{"conditionalSetIds":[],"forecasterId":"demographics-ai-2036:run1:inflation:reconciler","informationSetArtifactId":"sha256:8e70ac01d6f1107a777d6327bce2d370d149a12644631de260fb5f0a60b9c3e9","modelForecastIds":[],"modelUse":"none","prediction":{"kind":"quantiles","quantiles":[{"probability":0.1,"value":1.05},{"probability":0.5,"value":2},{"probability":0.9,"value":3.35}]},"questionHash":"sha256:20d8e05d3bea415eb4452ff8b599c74a3c3ce1a1b0c2ce11dda57a4e19490197","questionId":"demographics-ai-2036-cq4","questionVersion":"1.0.0","rationale":"WEIGHTING: Fermi heaviest (his anchor uses G7 2025-PPP weights summing to exactly 1.000 and his r* / term-premium / repression / measurement decomposition is the only additive ledger offered; he also caught that BOTH Inside-View weighted averages were computed on a 0.96 base, biasing that panelist's level down ~0.07 pp); Resolution Auditor heaviest on the measure audit; Red-Team PARTIALLY ADOPTED (one real hit, one pose).\n\nANCHOR: 0.515(2.60) + 0.117(0.40) + 0.105(0.50) + 0.079(1.60) + 0.076(1.15) + 0.062(2.00) + 0.046(1.65) = 1.852%.\n\nLEDGER. r* deltas: life-cycle dissaving as the old-age ratio goes 31 -> 40 pp, +0.35; public dissaving through the r* channel, +0.05; AI/grid capex demand for savings 0.34(+0.25) + 0.66(-0.20) = -0.05, i.e. the locked 66% bust puts the expected sign NEGATIVE inside my window; lower g from the care/physical cap and the China contraction, -0.35; precautionary saving, -0.15; income shifting to capital-concentrated, higher-saving holders, -0.10. NET r* = -0.25. Real term premium +0.55 (gross public debt >100% of GDP by 2029, ~142% US and ~127% China by 2031, net interest 2% -> 3% of GDP, P95 3-yr Debt-at-Risk 117% and +2.4 pp under a 20% AI equity shock, eroding sovereign convenience yields, marginal duration absorbed by levered basis trades that de-risk procyclically rather than by price-insensitive real money, DB plans turning from duration buyers into net payers, BoJ normalization lifting the JGB leg)